Z||000000||bcwawright||05-14-2001||07:31 PM||||Has anybody put power steering in. I have an 88GT with 2 steering dampers(needed because of bigger wheels and track increase) and its a bear to turn under 10mph.<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo F355 Replica||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||05-14-2001||10:46 PM||||With my 3800SC, I was think about it. Seems to me that the 80-81 X body power racks mount the same way. The input shaft from the steering wheel might be the wrong length. I already have the pump on the engine.<P>On a 2.8L engine, finding a place to mount the pump might be interesting but then there's no reason the X/A body brackets wouldn't work. 85-86 MPFI engines. PS, AC, alternator.<P>Hmmm, makes one think, donit?<P>Oh wait, 88. Does it mount the same as the 87-?<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 05-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||05-14-2001||10:53 PM||||I have been trying to figure this one out too.  It seems to me that if you have a engine swap with the power steering pump on it you should be able to run the line to the front.  There are several racks that could be used, one has to fit with a few mods, I mean if you can swap a motor, how hard is it to figure out.  The big prob that I see is where do you start with the racks???  But I have no doubt that the first one to figure this one out will make lots of money, I would pay big $$$ for power steering.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||05-15-2001||08:26 AM||||I was at a show at Englishtown NJ last weekend and a guy had a rebodied Fiero with power steering.  The rack was from a kit he had purchased from a firm I cannot remember. The rack was a modified Mercury Merkur according to him.  The kit included  a power steering pump and mounting for the 2.8.  He said he will be a Carlisle this weekend.||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||05-15-2001||10:58 AM||||You'll find a TON of info on this topic if you do a search. Rodney Dickman has PS on one of his cars. It was a kit that was offered at one time and uses a steering rack from a Mercury Meckur(sp?). I've toyed with the idea as a project several times myself but most days, It doesn't bother me enough to pursue it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||3
Z||000005||Slammed Fiero||05-15-2001||11:26 AM||||I have seen a few corvairs with Power Steering setup (Mid engine v8 vairs) The guys use a Mustang rack , run an underdrive pulley ont he pump to make up for the distance between the pump and the rack.<P>I would look at a lotus Esprit system<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
