Z||000008||skitime||05-15-2001||12:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bcwawright:<BR><B> Hey <BR>Are you going to Carlisle?????<BR>If so get me some more info and I'll buy you a beer or two.<BR>Thanks<P>Bruce<BR>88GT Turbo F355 Spyder replica<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, I will be there and I will try to get more information.  A picture of the car is on 84 Bills site.  <A HREF="http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Etown.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://cn308598-a.wall1.pa.home.com/fiero/Etown.htm</A>  It is the red Ferrari car.  If I remember the guys name was Dave, maybe someone knows him.  He put the kit on himself. I could use a beer or two for sure.||||reg||1
Z||000009||opm2000||05-15-2001||12:34 PM||||I have a remanufactured power steering rack from an '85 Chevette, cost $150.   I'm mounting it in my rebody project.   I'm using the powersteering pump on the LT1 engine.   This pump has a remote resivor, so you might consider this pump as a viable add on for a stock Fiero installation.<P>   The mounting points for the rack have to be modified somewhat.   The rack is shorter, so the rod ends/arms have to be modified somewhat.   The attach point between the rack and the Fiero steering column is moved over some, so the firewall hole has to be modified somewhat.   The couplings are different on the rack and the Fiero steering column, so a custom coupling has to be made up.<P>   If your putting monster tires on the front end, and giving it to your wife for a daily driver, I can understand doing all of this.<P>   If you are driving a fairly stock Fiero, I think you are a brute for punishment.<P>   Photos and a more complete write up can be found on the Diablo builder's Forum.<P>David Breeze<BR>N777H||||reg||14
Z||000010||Jefrysuko||05-15-2001||07:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfixit58:<BR><B>You'll find a TON of info on this topic if you do a search. Rodney Dickman has PS on one of his cars. It was a kit that was offered at one time and uses a steering rack from a Mercury Meckur(sp?). I've toyed with the idea as a project several times myself but most days, It doesn't bother me enough to pursue it.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Rodney has powersteering on his MERA.  The rack is from a Zimmer and your right it was a modified mercury mercur rack.  If I remember right at one time he had a spare unit.<P>Jeffrey D Suckow<BR>88 GT<BR>||||reg||1
